@page "/task-list/calendar"

<PageTitle>Task calendar — Backlog UI Storybook</PageTitle>

<StoryPage Title="Task calendar"
           Summary="`TaskCalendar`: a month of tasks placed by their due date, Monday-first and in whole weeks, with the open tasks that have no due date in a tray beside it. A chip or a tray item opens its task; dragging one onto a day gives it that due date. The roadmap's plans can be drawn over it: each window a bar across its days, each milestone a diamond, and the plans with no window yet in the tray. Hours the person sets aside for a task on a day are chips of their own, added up against the day's working hours. The Tasks pane that hands it the filtered rows is not this page's subject."
           Guidelines="@Rules">

    <Story Name="A month of tasks"
           Description="`Tasks` is every task the host's filters let through, each a `CalendarTask` with its due date, its state and the host's repository mark. The month bar steps back and forward and returns to today's month. The weeks run Monday to Sunday and reach into the neighbouring months, whose days are dimmed; Saturday and Sunday are shaded. Today's number is ringed and the cell says how many tasks are in My Day, from `MyDayCount`.

A day shows two chips and folds the rest behind `+N more`, which opens the whole day in place. An open task due before `Today` is drawn in the error colour; a done one is struck through. The dot says the state in shape as well as colour: a hollow ring for a draft.

Drag a chip to another day, or a tray item onto a day: the line under the sample says what the host was told. A press that does not travel opens the task instead."
           Code="@MonthCode">
        <div class="sb-calendar" data-testid="task-calendar-month">
            <TaskCalendar Tasks="@_tasks"
                          Today="@Today"
                          MyDayCount="2"
                          SelectedId="@_opened"
                          OnOpen="Open"
                          OnDueChanged="Move"
                          TestId="calendar" />
        </div>
        <p class="sb-state" data-testid="task-calendar-state">@(_lastEvent ?? "Nothing opened or moved yet.")</p>
    </Story>

    <Story Name="The repository identity edge"
           Description="The edge is the host's, through each task's `CssClass`, on the seam a list row and a board card use: the desktop pane passes the shared `repo-mark repo-mark--N` classes while its repository colours are showing and nothing when they are off. The calendar never decides whether the colours are on. The switch below plays the host."
           Code="@EdgeCode">
        <label class="sb-row">
            <input type="checkbox" checked="@_colours" @onchange="e => _colours = e.Value is true" data-testid="task-calendar-colours" />
            Repository colours
        </label>
        <div class="sb-calendar" data-testid="task-calendar-edges">
            <TaskCalendar Tasks="@EdgeTasks"
                          Today="@Today"
                          TestId="edges" />
        </div>
    </Story>

    <Story Name="Calendar with plans"
           Description="With `PlansAvailable` the month bar carries a **Show plans** box, ticked by default; the host keeps the choice (`ShowPlans`, `ShowPlansChanged`). Each `CalendarPlan` is a bar across the days of its window, cut at every week row, under the day numbers and above the chips. Plans that overlap in a week take a lane each, and the week makes room for its lanes. A bar carried on from the week before opens with `…`. Hover a bar: the tooltip gives the title, the plan tag and the finished points of the total.

The fill is the plan's band colour at the roadmap's 24% mix while the host passes a `Band` — only while its repository colours are showing — and neutral grey otherwise; the switch below plays the host. Each `CalendarMilestone` is a diamond chip on its day.

The tray's second section, **Plans without a window**, lists the `ShelfPlans`. Drag one onto a day: the calendar reports `OnPlanStarted` with the tag and the day, and sizes nothing. In the app the roadmap places the window from that day by its own placement; here the host stands in with a window of the plan's points at five a week, so the drop can be seen landing."
           Code="@PlansCode">
        <label class="sb-row">
            <input type="checkbox" checked="@_planColours" @onchange="e => _planColours = e.Value is true" data-testid="task-calendar-plan-colours" />
            Repository colours
        </label>
        <div class="sb-calendar" data-testid="task-calendar-plans">
            <TaskCalendar Tasks="@_tasks"
                          Today="@Today"
                          MyDayCount="2"
                          PlansAvailable="true"
                          ShowPlans="@_showPlans"
                          ShowPlansChanged="shown => _showPlans = shown"
                          Plans="@Plans"
                          Milestones="@Milestones"
                          ShelfPlans="@_shelf"
                          OnPlanStarted="StartPlan"
                          TestId="plans" />
        </div>
        <p class="sb-state" data-testid="task-calendar-plans-state">@(_planEvent ?? "No plan started yet.")</p>
    </Story>

    <Story Name="Planned hours"
           Description="With `HoursAvailable` the person can set hours aside for a task on a day — a date and a number of hours, never a time of day. Each `CalendarHoursBlock` is a chip on its day, **Title · 3h**, dashed and tinted with a bar for a mark, apart from the solid due-date chips. The day head adds the day's blocks up against what `CapacityOn` says the day has — **3h / 8h** — and a day holding more is drawn in the error colour, its tooltip naming the numbers: the 12th here, and the Saturday with no working hours.

Make a block from a day's **Add hours…** (it shows while the day is pointed at or focused), or drag a chip or a tray item onto a day with **Shift** held. Either opens the day's editor; press a block's chip to change or remove it. The calendar reports `OnHoursChanged` and writes nothing — here the host keeps the blocks in memory. The roadmap never reads them.

Under it, `PlannedHoursEditor`: the same blocks for one task, as the Tasks detail panel's **Planned hours** section edits them."
           Code="@HoursCode">
        <div class="sb-calendar" data-testid="task-calendar-hours">
            <TaskCalendar Tasks="@_tasks"
                          Today="@Today"
                          MyDayCount="2"
                          HoursAvailable="true"
                          HoursBlocks="@HoursBlocks"
                          CapacityOn="CapacityOn"
                          OnHoursChanged="ChangeHours"
                          TestId="hours" />
        </div>
        <p class="sb-state" data-testid="task-calendar-hours-state">@(_hoursEvent ?? "No hours planned or changed yet.")</p>
        <div class="sb-panel" data-testid="planned-hours-panel">
            <PlannedHoursEditor Blocks="@PanelBlocks"
                                DefaultDay="@Today"
                                OnChanged="change => ChangeHours(new CalendarHoursChange(PanelTaskId, change.On, change.Hours))"
                                TestId="planned-hours" />
        </div>
    </Story>

    <Story Name="An empty tray"
           Description="With every open task dated, the tray says so rather than vanishing — it is where the next undated task will appear, and a drop target the reader has already learned the place of."
           Code="@EmptyCode">
        <div class="sb-calendar" data-testid="task-calendar-empty">
            <TaskCalendar Tasks="@([.. _tasks.Where(task => task.DueOn is not null)])"
                          Today="@Today"
                          TestId="empty" />
        </div>
    </Story>
</StoryPage>

@code {
    private static readonly DesignGuideline[] Rules =
    [
        new("interaction-guidelines.md#drag-and-drop-reordering", "Why a drag is a pointer gesture with a threshold, and what a press that does not travel stays."),
        new("color-scheme.md#the-identity-edge", "The 4px repository edge, and that it is never the only thing naming the repository."),
        new("accessibility.md#iconography-accessibility", "Why a status dot differs in shape as well as colour.")
    ];

    /// <summary>A fixed today, so the page reads the same on every day it is opened.</summary>
    private static readonly DateOnly Today = new(2026, 10, 6);

    private List<CalendarTask> _tasks =
    [
        new("hours", "Hours report shows prompt count", new DateOnly(2026, 9, 30), CalendarTaskState.Done, Effort: "2 pts"),
        new("rotate", "Rotate the sync signing key", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 1), CalendarTaskState.Ready, CssClass: "repo-mark repo-mark--3"),
        new("dedupe", "Import plan dedupes by id", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 2), CalendarTaskState.Done),
        new("review", "Review merge feedback", Today, CalendarTaskState.InProgress, Repeats: true),
        new("retro", "Weekly retro", Today, CalendarTaskState.Ready, Repeats: true),
        new("card", "Extract TaskCard from TaskItem", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 8), CalendarTaskState.InProgress, CssClass: "repo-mark repo-mark--1"),
        new("switch", "Shared view switcher", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 9), CalendarTaskState.Ready, CssClass: "repo-mark repo-mark--1"),
        new("columns", "Board view: status columns", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 16), CalendarTaskState.Ready),
        new("flow", "Drag follows status flow", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 16), CalendarTaskState.Ready),
        new("notes", "Release notes for task views", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 16), CalendarTaskState.Draft),
        new("calendar", "Calendar view by due date", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 23), CalendarTaskState.Draft),
        new("release", "Release 0.9", new DateOnly(2026, 11, 1), CalendarTaskState.Draft),
        new("swimlanes", "Explore swimlanes by plan on the board", null, CalendarTaskState.Draft),
        new("persist", "Persist the last view per workspace", null, CalendarTaskState.Ready, Effort: "1 pt"),
        new("keyboard", "Move a task one day with Alt+Arrow", null, CalendarTaskState.Ready, Effort: "2 pts")
    ];

    private string? _opened;
    private string? _lastEvent;
    private bool _colours = true;

    private bool _showPlans = true;
    private bool _planColours = true;
    private string? _planEvent;

    private List<(string Id, string Title, string Tag, DateOnly Start, DateOnly End, int Done, int Total, int Band)> _plans =
    [
        ("views", "Task views", "task-views", new DateOnly(2026, 9, 30), new DateOnly(2026, 10, 14), 13, 34, 1),
        ("calendar", "Calendar plans", "calendar-plans", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 8), new DateOnly(2026, 10, 20), 0, 8, 2),
        ("sync", "Sync devices", "sync-devices", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 13), new DateOnly(2026, 10, 16), 2, 5, 3)
    ];

    private List<CalendarShelfPlan> _shelf =
    [
        new("release-q4", "Release q4", TaskCount: 4, TotalEffort: 10, UnestimatedCount: 1),
        new("docs-refresh", "Docs refresh", TaskCount: 2, TotalEffort: 3)
    ];

    private IReadOnlyList<CalendarPlan> Plans =>
    [
        .. _plans.Select(plan => new CalendarPlan(
            plan.Id, plan.Title, plan.Tag, plan.Start, plan.End, plan.Done, plan.Total,
            _planColours ? plan.Band : null))
    ];

    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<CalendarMilestone> Milestones =
    [
        new("beta", "Beta", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 16)),
        new("release", "Release 0.9", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 30))
    ];

    /// <summary>Plays the host: in the app the roadmap places the window; here it is the
    /// plan's points at five a week, whole days, from the day it was dropped on.</summary>
    private void StartPlan(CalendarPlanStart start)
    {
        var plan = _shelf.FirstOrDefault(candidate => candidate.Tag == start.Tag);
        if (plan is null) return;

        var days = Math.Max(1, (int)Math.Ceiling(plan.TotalEffort / 5m * 7));
        _shelf = [.. _shelf.Where(candidate => candidate.Tag != start.Tag)];
        _plans = [.. _plans, (plan.Tag, plan.Title, plan.Tag, start.Start, start.Start.AddDays(days - 1), 0, plan.TotalEffort, 4)];
        _planEvent = $"Started +{plan.Tag} on {start.Start:yyyy-MM-dd}.";
    }

    private IReadOnlyList<CalendarTask> EdgeTasks =>
    [
        new("edge-1", "Filed against backlog", Today.AddDays(1), CalendarTaskState.Ready, CssClass: _colours ? "repo-mark repo-mark--1" : null),
        new("edge-2", "Filed against backlog-sync", Today.AddDays(1), CalendarTaskState.InProgress, CssClass: _colours ? "repo-mark repo-mark--2" : null),
        new("edge-3", "Not dated yet", null, CalendarTaskState.Draft, CssClass: _colours ? "repo-mark repo-mark--3" : null)
    ];

    private void Open(string id)
    {
        _opened = id;
        _lastEvent = $"Opened {Title(id)}.";
    }

    private void Move(CalendarDueChange change)
    {
        var index = _tasks.FindIndex(task => task.Id == change.TaskId);
        if (index < 0) return;

        _tasks[index] = _tasks[index] with { DueOn = change.DueOn };
        _tasks = [.. _tasks];
        _lastEvent = $"Moved {Title(change.TaskId)} to {change.DueOn:yyyy-MM-dd}.";
    }

    // --- Planned hours ------------------------------------------------------------

    private const string PanelTaskId = "card";

    private string? _hoursEvent;

    private List<(string TaskId, DateOnly On, decimal Hours)> _hours =
    [
        ("card", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 7), 3m),
        ("switch", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 7), 2m),
        ("card", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 12), 5m),
        ("columns", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 12), 4m),
        ("persist", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 10), 1.5m),
        ("review", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 14), 0.5m)
    ];

    private IReadOnlyList<CalendarHoursBlock> HoursBlocks =>
    [
        .. _hours.Select(held => new CalendarHoursBlock(
            held.TaskId,
            Title(held.TaskId),
            held.On,
            held.Hours,
            _tasks.FirstOrDefault(task => task.Id == held.TaskId)?.CssClass))
    ];

    private IReadOnlyList<PlannedHoursDay> PanelBlocks =>
        [.. _hours.Where(held => held.TaskId == PanelTaskId).OrderBy(held => held.On).Select(held => new PlannedHoursDay(held.On, held.Hours))];

    /// <summary>Plays the roadmap's working week: eight hours Monday to Friday, none at
    /// the weekend, and a half day on the 13th.</summary>
    private static decimal? CapacityOn(DateOnly day) =>
        day.DayOfWeek is DayOfWeek.Saturday or DayOfWeek.Sunday ? 0m
        : day == new DateOnly(2026, 10, 13) ? 4m
        : 8m;

    private void ChangeHours(CalendarHoursChange change)
    {
        _hours = [.. _hours.Where(held => !(held.TaskId == change.TaskId && held.On == change.On))];
        if (change.Hours is { } hours) _hours.Add((change.TaskId, change.On, hours));
        _hoursEvent = change.Hours is { } figure
            ? $"Planned {figure}h for {Title(change.TaskId)} on {change.On:yyyy-MM-dd}."
            : $"Removed the hours for {Title(change.TaskId)} on {change.On:yyyy-MM-dd}.";
    }

    private const string HoursCode = """
        <TaskCalendar Tasks="@tasks"
                      Today="@today"
                      HoursAvailable="true"
                      HoursBlocks="@blocks"
                      CapacityOn="day => workingWeek.HoursOn(day)"
                      OnHoursChanged="change => backlog.SetPlannedHoursAsync(change.TaskId, change.On, change.Hours)" />

        <PlannedHoursEditor Blocks="@blocksOfOneTask"
                            DefaultDay="@today"
                            OnChanged="change => backlog.SetPlannedHoursAsync(taskId, change.On, change.Hours)" />

        @code {
            // A day and a number of hours; null hours on a change removes the day's block.
            IReadOnlyList<CalendarHoursBlock> blocks =
            [
                new("card", "Extract TaskCard from TaskItem", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 7), 3m)
            ];
        }
        """;

    private string Title(string id) => _tasks.FirstOrDefault(task => task.Id == id)?.Title ?? id;

    private const string MonthCode = """
        <TaskCalendar Tasks="@tasks"
                      Today="@today"
                      MyDayCount="@myDayCount"
                      SelectedId="@openId"
                      OnOpen="Open"
                      OnDueChanged="change => SetDue(change.TaskId, change.DueOn)" />

        @code {
            // One record per task the filters let through.
            IReadOnlyList<CalendarTask> tasks =
            [
                new("rotate", "Rotate the sync signing key", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 1), CalendarTaskState.Ready),
                new("dedupe", "Import plan dedupes by id", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 2), CalendarTaskState.Done),
                new("persist", "Persist the last view per workspace", null, CalendarTaskState.Ready, Effort: "1 pt")
            ];
        }
        """;

    private const string EdgeCode = """
        <TaskCalendar Tasks="@tasks" Today="@today" />

        @code {
            // The host's own answer, passed only while its colours are showing.
            CalendarTask Of(Entry entry) => new(
                entry.Id, entry.Title, entry.DueOn, entry.State,
                CssClass: coloursShowing ? $"repo-mark repo-mark--{entry.Colour}" : null);
        }
        """;

    private const string PlansCode = """
        <TaskCalendar Tasks="@tasks"
                      Today="@today"
                      PlansAvailable="true"
                      @bind-ShowPlans="showPlans"
                      Plans="@plans"
                      Milestones="@milestones"
                      ShelfPlans="@shelf"
                      OnPlanStarted="start => roadmap.StartAsync(start.Tag, start.Start)" />

        @code {
            // Band only while the repository colours are showing; null draws neutral grey.
            IReadOnlyList<CalendarPlan> plans =
            [
                new("views", "Task views", "task-views",
                    new DateOnly(2026, 9, 30), new DateOnly(2026, 10, 14),
                    DonePoints: 13, TotalPoints: 34, Band: 1)
            ];

            IReadOnlyList<CalendarMilestone> milestones = [new("beta", "Beta", new DateOnly(2026, 10, 16))];

            IReadOnlyList<CalendarShelfPlan> shelf =
                [new("release-q4", "Release q4", TaskCount: 4, TotalEffort: 10, UnestimatedCount: 1)];
        }
        """;

    private const string EmptyCode = """
        <TaskCalendar Tasks="@datedTasks" Today="@today" />
        """;
}
